That would be the CwnAnnwn (or Cwn Annwn) - translated as the Hounds of
Hell, or as the Hounds of Annwn, as if Annwn is a proper name. I don't
speak Welsh, so I don't know which is more accurate. In any case, yes,
they're Welsh, they're not _a_ monster but a group, and their howling is
a portent of death. They're white-coated, red-eared, and take part in
the Wild Hunt.
It means you've got fewer than a tenth of your maximum hit points left,
but more than one. If you'd had only one HP left, you'd heard "the
wailing of the Banshee", which is appropriate, because while the call of
the Cwn Annwn is a sign of grave danger, the keening of the Bean Sidhe
is a sign that someone is actually about to die.
If you'd been an Elf, a Valkyrie, or a Wizard, you'd have seen a line
from Gauntlet, instead.

